- Right. - including the commentating.

1304
00:53:36,777 --> 00:53:38,917
(He does horseback riding as a hobby instead of work now.)

1305
00:53:40,977 --> 00:53:45,187
(He gets properly dressed.)

1306
00:53:47,417 --> 00:53:49,427
(He even puts on his helmet!)

1307
00:53:52,397 --> 00:53:53,496
Gosh, that's impressive!

1308
00:53:53,497 --> 00:53:55,356
Gosh!

1309
00:53:55,357 --> 00:53:57,527
You look like a foreign equestrian.

1310
00:53:58,197 --> 00:53:59,696
You have really long legs.

1311
00:53:59,697 --> 00:54:01,166
- Right. - The outfit looks nice.

1312
00:54:01,167 --> 00:54:02,806
- The outfits look nice. - Right.

1313
00:54:02,807 --> 00:54:05,836
You need the right equipment for horseback riding.

1314
00:54:05,837 --> 00:54:08,606
I have all of the equipment.

1315
00:54:08,607 --> 00:54:09,706
- You need the equipment. - You have your own equipment?

1316
00:54:09,707 --> 00:54:11,847
Yes. Back then, I thought it was an investment.

1317
00:54:12,077 --> 00:54:13,876
It was an investment...

1318
00:54:13,877 --> 00:54:15,786
- to get into that field. - This is what it feels like today.

1319
00:54:15,787 --> 00:54:17,186
It feels like you're trying to explain yourself.

1320
00:54:17,187 --> 00:54:19,556
It's not a hearing today.

1321
00:54:19,557 --> 00:54:20,787
- There's no need to be like that. - First,

1322
00:54:20,987 --> 00:54:22,727
- say that you're sorry. - Right.

1323
00:54:22,927 --> 00:54:24,326
I apologize for drinking wine.

1324
00:54:24,327 --> 00:54:25,526
No! What's wrong with that?

1325
00:54:25,527 --> 00:54:27,356
- I apologize for horseback riding. - Genesis.

1326
00:54:27,357 --> 00:54:28,427
Right.

1327
00:54:28,527 --> 00:54:29,796
I apologize for driving a Genesis.

1328
00:54:29,797 --> 00:54:31,896
You don't have to explain yourself. Be confident.

1329
00:54:31,897 --> 00:54:33,367
- Of course. - Understood.

1330
00:54:34,797 --> 00:54:37,537
(He confidently gets his equipment.)

1331
00:54:39,307 --> 00:54:41,306
I bought some carrots for the horses.

1332
00:54:41,307 --> 00:54:43,447
- I see. - Gosh, thank you so much.

1333
00:54:43,547 --> 00:54:44,547
Right.

1334
00:54:45,077 --> 00:54:47,146
- Cookie! Gosh, Cookie. - Yes.

1335
00:54:47,147 --> 00:54:48,147
(Have you been doing well, Cookie?)

1336
00:54:48,277 --> 00:54:49,616
Are you renting a horse as well?

1337
00:54:49,617 --> 00:54:51,286
- From the stable. - A rented horse.

1338
00:54:51,287 --> 00:54:53,987
The horses have their own owners.

1339
00:54:54,257 --> 00:54:55,986
I'm riding the horses there.

1340
00:54:55,987 --> 00:54:57,987
- They all have their owners. - Right.

1341
00:54:58,187 --> 00:55:00,227
Hey, Cookie.

1342
00:55:00,857 --> 00:55:04,066
Cookie is a horse that I got on several times.

1343
00:55:04,067 --> 00:55:05,167
- I see. - Right.

1344
00:55:05,697 --> 00:55:06,966
Cookie looks so pretty.

1345
00:55:06,967 --> 00:55:09,407
Gosh, you want some don't you?

1346
00:55:09,667 --> 00:55:12,137
(I brought carrots, Cookie.)

1347
00:55:12,237 --> 00:55:14,277
Do you want some? Here you are.

1348
00:55:15,337 --> 00:55:16,777
(Crunch)

1349
00:55:17,047 --> 00:55:18,047
(Chewing)

1350
00:55:18,048 --> 00:55:19,277
Cookie is enjoying it.

1351
00:55:20,717 --> 00:55:22,616
(The horse seems to be grateful for Woo Il's efforts.)

1352
00:55:22,617 --> 00:55:23,617
- Gosh! - Cookie is really enjoying it.

1353
00:55:23,618 --> 00:55:25,716
The horse looks fascinating. It's like a giraffe.

1354
00:55:25,717 --> 00:55:26,817
The horse looks pretty.

1355
00:55:27,017 --> 00:55:28,057
Okay.

1356
00:55:29,087 --> 00:55:31,687
(It's good.)

1357
00:55:31,727 --> 00:55:34,426
After a few months,

1358
00:55:34,427 --> 00:55:36,567
the horses felt like dogs.

1359
00:55:36,697 --> 00:55:37,996
(Connecting)

1360
00:55:37,997 --> 00:55:39,537
You can connect with a horse...

1361
00:55:39,867 --> 00:55:42,707
just like a dog.

1362
00:55:45,337 --> 00:55:47,737
Have all of it.

1363
00:55:48,847 --> 00:55:50,276
(Sweet)

1364
00:55:50,277 --> 00:55:51,977
Got it? Have some more after chewing everything.

1365
00:55:52,977 --> 00:55:55,587
We have to do well together. Got it?

1366
00:55:55,717 --> 00:55:57,346
- We have to do well together. - It's a meek horse.

1367
00:55:57,347 --> 00:55:58,387
Got it?

1368
00:56:00,317 --> 00:56:02,186
Okay. There we go.

1369
00:56:02,187 --> 00:56:04,187
(Let's get some exercise now that we've connected.)

1370
00:56:05,357 --> 00:56:08,597
(He heads into the training center full of excitement.)

1371
00:56:09,667 --> 00:56:11,466
(He moves to the other side of Cookie.)

1372
00:56:11,467 --> 00:56:13,367
All right.

1373
00:56:13,867 --> 00:56:14,997
Hey, Cookie.

1374
00:56:15,607 --> 00:56:16,707
Hey, Cookie.

1375
00:56:16,807 --> 00:56:17,906
- Hey, Cookie. - Hold the reins.

1376
00:56:17,907 --> 00:56:19,577
(The man who gets on the white horse)

1377
00:56:19,677 --> 00:56:20,977
(Bacterrius)

1378
00:56:21,037 --> 00:56:23,777
(Terrius)

1379
00:56:23,847 --> 00:56:25,617
- "Bacterrius." - Terrius.

1380
00:56:26,077 --> 00:56:28,246
- You're not scared anymore, right? - No.

1381
00:56:28,247 --> 00:56:30,017
- It must be scary at first. - It does feel scary at first.

1382
00:56:30,087 --> 00:56:32,716
It feels like you're much higher up on the horse.

1383
00:56:32,717 --> 00:56:33,917
- Gosh. - Right.

1384
00:56:34,317 --> 00:56:36,926
- Okay. - The reins are ready.

1385
00:56:36,927 --> 00:56:38,227
- Walk. - Right.

1386
00:56:38,857 --> 00:56:39,897
All right.

1387
00:56:40,057 --> 00:56:41,726
(Let's go!)

1388
00:56:41,727 --> 00:56:42,767
Forward.

1389
00:56:43,767 --> 00:56:46,137
- Cookie must be a good horse. - Right.

1390
00:56:46,567 --> 00:56:49,137
- Walk comfortably. - Right.

1391
00:56:50,567 --> 00:56:52,937
(They start with a simple warmup.)

1392
00:56:54,427 --> 00:56:56,321
He looks like a prince of a country.

1393
00:56:58,177 --> 00:57:00,777
(The warm sunlight shines through the windows.)

1394
00:57:01,817 --> 00:57:04,747
(The prince on the white horse moves gracefully.)

1395
00:57:06,017 --> 00:57:07,017
(Am I the one to become King?)

1396
00:57:07,018 --> 00:57:08,217
It's a great sight.

1397
00:57:10,957 --> 00:57:13,857
Walking is the simplest form of moving.

1398
00:57:13,927 --> 00:57:16,467
I give signals to the horse with my foot.

1399
00:57:16,697 --> 00:57:18,867
I give a single kick during the walk.

1400
00:57:20,067 --> 00:57:21,967
The trot is next.

1401
00:57:22,197 --> 00:57:24,066
The trot is like a power walk.

1402
00:57:24,067 --> 00:57:26,007
It's a faster walk.

1403
00:57:26,237 --> 00:57:27,876
Your back has to be like that.

1404
00:57:27,877 --> 00:57:29,507
I have to bounce up and down like that.

1405
00:57:29,807 --> 00:57:31,646
- I have to move like that. - That's fascinating.

1406
00:57:31,647 --> 00:57:33,147
You'll hurt your back if you don't do that.

1407
00:57:33,317 --> 00:57:35,246
That also makes the horse...

1408
00:57:35,247 --> 00:57:36,547
- feel less exhausted. - Right.

1409
00:57:36,717 --> 00:57:40,457
Moving up and down helps the horse move better.

1410
00:57:40,587 --> 00:57:41,616
That's impressive.

1411
00:57:41,617 --> 00:57:43,556
I'm not just sitting comfortably on the horse.

1412
00:57:43,557 --> 00:57:45,997
I have to stay fixed on the horse with my thighs.

1413
00:57:46,597 --> 00:57:48,326
Your adductor muscles have to suffer so much.

1414
00:57:48,327 --> 00:57:50,097
I constantly have to strain my lower body.

1415
00:57:50,367 --> 00:57:51,627
It brings up your hips as well.

1416
00:57:52,667 --> 00:57:53,996
I heard horseback riding is great for women.

1417
00:57:53,997 --> 00:57:55,437
Right.

1418
00:57:56,437 --> 00:57:57,766
Keep going.

1419
00:57:57,767 --> 00:57:59,637
(The adductor muscles are fixed as he moves his back.)

1420
00:58:00,007 --> 00:58:03,077
(He works on the pace with Cookie.)

1421
00:58:03,907 --> 00:58:06,646
- Check the direction. - Gosh.

1422
00:58:06,647 --> 00:58:07,977
- His hair is flying in the air. - Good.

1423
00:58:09,417 --> 00:58:11,387
Let's warm up outside.

1424
00:58:12,757 --> 00:58:14,256
(Groaning)

1425
00:58:14,257 --> 00:58:16,027
My back is hurting already.

1426
00:58:17,187 --> 00:58:19,096
(They move outside.)

1427
00:58:19,097 --> 00:58:21,427
- Do the same thing outside. - Right.

1428
00:58:21,757 --> 00:58:23,667
- Let's go. - It feels like England.

1429
00:58:24,297 --> 00:58:25,496
You look like a nobleman!

1430
00:58:25,497 --> 00:58:26,997
- It feels like Buckingham. - Right.

1431
00:58:29,207 --> 00:58:31,507
- Shall we go with the canter now? - Okay.

1432
00:58:32,317 --> 00:58:33,586
(Let's go, Cookie!)

1433
00:58:33,587 --> 00:58:34,656
There you go.

1434
00:58:34,657 --> 00:58:36,457
I give all of the signals with my foot.

1435
00:58:36,887 --> 00:58:39,027
(The canter begins with his signal.)

1436
00:58:40,757 --> 00:58:43,927
(Cookie picks up the pace.)

1437
00:58:45,697 --> 00:58:48,037
(Moving up and down)

1438
00:58:49,437 --> 00:58:51,036
(The canter is done with a stable form.)

1439
00:58:51,037 --> 00:58:53,476
- I did some running today. - Gosh.

1440
00:58:53,477 --> 00:58:55,176
Look at you.

1441
00:58:55,177 --> 00:58:56,376
He's good at this.

1442
00:58:56,377 --> 00:58:58,176
Your form looks great.

1443
00:58:58,177 --> 00:59:00,517
- You're doing well. - Well, he did do it for a year.

1444
00:59:01,677 --> 00:59:02,846
Right. Just like that.

1445
00:59:02,847 --> 00:59:05,446
(The one who rides through the open field)

1446
00:59:05,447 --> 00:59:07,817
(Terrius on a white horse)

1447
00:59:09,027 --> 00:59:12,797
(Don't fall asleep, Princess.)

1448
00:59:14,327 --> 00:59:15,896
(I am right here.)

1449
00:59:15,897 --> 00:59:17,196
Enjoy it even more.

1450
00:59:17,197 --> 00:59:19,167
(Hair flying in the air)

1451
00:59:21,497 --> 00:59:22,767
You look like a rich man!

1452
00:59:23,707 --> 00:59:25,636
(Did he buy a white horse with his own money?)

1453
00:59:25,637 --> 00:59:26,877
It's like "The Rose of Versailles."

1454
00:59:27,477 --> 00:59:30,176
- He's just like Terrius today. - On his way to meet the princess.

1455
00:59:30,177 --> 00:59:31,377
(Terrius)

1456
00:59:32,007 --> 00:59:34,047
(Will you not hurry?)

1457
00:59:34,717 --> 00:59:36,647
(I'm on my way to meet the princess!)

1458
00:59:38,147 --> 00:59:40,657
Rest and turn. Warm up.

1459
00:59:41,617 --> 00:59:43,027
Slowly.

1460
00:59:44,257 --> 00:59:45,927
- Your form looks good today. - Great job.

1461
00:59:46,427 --> 00:59:47,627
Gosh, this is exhausting.

1462
00:59:48,097 --> 00:59:49,867
The prince on the white horse lacks so much stamina.

1463
00:59:50,627 --> 00:59:53,637
That was just the warmup.

1464
00:59:55,297 --> 00:59:56,937
The course we did the other time.

1465
00:59:57,137 --> 00:59:58,976
Let's go through that course.

1466
00:59:58,977 --> 01:00:01,377
Go around and go to number two toward the end.

1467
01:00:02,137 --> 01:00:03,276
You're going over obstacles?

1468
01:00:03,277 --> 01:00:05,446
- You're doing that? - That must be really hard to do.

1469
01:00:05,447 --> 01:00:07,317
It's hard to memorize the order.

1470
01:00:08,477 --> 01:00:10,686
(There are various obstacles with numbers.)

1471
01:00:10,687 --> 01:00:13,616
It's really confusing to memorize the course.

1472
01:00:13,617 --> 01:00:17,027
I have to go to number 1 and turn to go to number 7.

1473
01:00:17,157 --> 01:00:18,426
I have to move back and forth with the same obstacle.

1474
01:00:18,427 --> 01:00:20,156
- You have to be smart to do this. - Right.

1475
01:00:20,157 --> 01:00:21,826
So before I start,

1476
01:00:21,827 --> 01:00:25,067
I go around the course to show the horse.

1477
01:00:25,197 --> 01:00:27,236
"You go here and there."

1478
01:00:27,237 --> 01:00:29,506
- Just like for dogs. - Dog agility?

1479
01:00:29,507 --> 01:00:32,136
- Right. The dogs go here and there. - Just like that?

1480
01:00:32,137 --> 01:00:34,236
- Dog agility. - Just like that,

1481
01:00:34,237 --> 01:00:35,306
- I show the horse what to do. - When you get it wrong,

1482
01:00:35,307 --> 01:00:36,776
you know how you must do it until you get it correct, right?

1483
01:00:36,777 --> 01:00:37,847
Right.

1484
01:00:38,047 --> 01:00:40,377
It's just the same. The horses need to be told as well.

1485
01:00:41,077 --> 01:00:43,747
Number 1, number 2, number 3.

1486
01:00:45,347 --> 01:00:47,656
(Scanning carefully)

1487
01:00:47,657 --> 01:00:48,817
Number four. Okay.

1488
01:00:49,727 --> 01:00:50,786
Let's go.

1489
01:00:50,787 --> 01:00:53,027
(Let's go, Cookie!)

1490
01:00:54,097 --> 01:00:56,797
Move out wide and look at number one.

1491
01:00:57,767 --> 01:00:59,597
Wider. There you go.

1492
01:01:01,197 --> 01:01:03,167
Jump over and turn right.

1493
01:01:03,537 --> 01:01:05,706
- That's impressive, Woo Il. - Turn right. Wider.

1494
01:01:05,707 --> 01:01:07,007
You don't have to speed up now.

1495
01:01:08,777 --> 01:01:10,018
Widen out the line.

1496
01:01:10,707 --> 01:01:12,206
There you go. Look at it and turn.

1497
01:01:12,207 --> 01:01:13,717
(He looks at obstacle number 2 this time.)

1498
01:01:14,877 --> 01:01:16,016
After a year of this,

1499
01:01:16,017 --> 01:01:18,146
- you can jump over obstacles. - Gosh!

1500
01:01:18,147 --> 01:01:19,156
Wide.

1501
01:01:19,157 --> 01:01:20,356
(He also passes obstacle number 2 with ease.)

1502
01:01:20,357 --> 01:01:21,857
There you go. Think of the next one.

1503
01:01:24,027 --> 01:01:25,386
(Groaning)

1504
01:01:25,387 --> 01:01:27,396
- Bring your shoulders back. - These are dangerous moments.

1505
01:01:27,397 --> 01:01:29,097
That's intense.

1506
01:01:29,467 --> 01:01:31,667
- They had to go over that one. - Gosh, he almost fell off.

1507
01:01:32,167 --> 01:01:33,296
- Gosh. - Gosh.

1508
01:01:33,297 --> 01:01:34,396
This is what happens.

1509
01:01:34,397 --> 01:01:36,407
You fall off if you lose your balance.

1510
01:01:37,637 --> 01:01:38,866
Gosh, this isn't easy.

1511
01:01:38,867 --> 01:01:41,806
The obstacles are set up like this.

1512
01:01:41,807 --> 01:01:43,606
The jump has to be done right in the middle...

1513
01:01:43,607 --> 01:01:45,447
for the horse not to get surprised.

1514
01:01:45,717 --> 01:01:47,446
- When we're toward the side, - The horse wouldn't jump.

1515
01:01:47,447 --> 01:01:50,116
it would see the block...

1516
01:01:50,117 --> 01:01:52,516
and make a sudden turn after being surprised.

1517
01:01:52,517 --> 01:01:54,517
- That's how people end up falling. - Gosh, that's scary!

1518
01:01:55,317 --> 01:01:57,727
(Focusing again)

1519
01:01:59,257 --> 01:02:00,856
Do it slowly. It doesn't have to be fast.

1520
01:02:00,857 --> 01:02:02,197
(He tries the course he failed once again.)

1521
01:02:03,797 --> 01:02:04,866
There you go. Bring your shoulders back.

1522
01:02:04,867 --> 01:02:05,936
Think of number three.

1523
01:02:05,937 --> 01:02:07,096
Slowly. Move your shoulder back.

1524
01:02:07,097 --> 01:02:08,866
- Gosh! - Slowly.

1525
01:02:08,867 --> 01:02:09,867
What's wrong?

1526
01:02:09,868 --> 01:02:11,336
- What's wrong? - What's wrong?

1527
01:02:11,337 --> 01:02:13,237
- The horse moved away. - It went the other way.

1528
01:02:14,377 --> 01:02:16,046
Have you ever fallen off a horse?

1529
01:02:16,047 --> 01:02:18,907
I have.

1530
01:02:19,077 --> 01:02:22,117
Wouldn't that traumatize you from doing it again?

1531
01:02:22,247 --> 01:02:24,746
Our rhythms didn't match.

1532
01:02:24,747 --> 01:02:26,557
The horse and I had to jump up at the same time,

1533
01:02:26,857 --> 01:02:28,416
- my bottom went up first... - Oh, gosh!

1534
01:02:28,417 --> 01:02:30,886
- and I was hit in mid-air. - You were hit?

1535
01:02:30,887 --> 01:02:33,056
- Gosh! - I fell sideways.

1536
01:02:33,057 --> 01:02:34,156
- Did you not get hurt? - I did get hurt.

1537
01:02:34,157 --> 01:02:35,196
- Where did you get hurt? - Where did you get hurt?

1538
01:02:35,197 --> 01:02:36,197
I hurt my shoulder.

1539
01:02:36,198 --> 01:02:37,226
I went to the hospital...

1540
01:02:37,227 --> 01:02:38,766
and I was told that my shoulder was fractured.

1541
01:02:38,767 --> 01:02:40,296
- Gosh! - Right.

1542
01:02:40,297 --> 01:02:43,107
- You're really high up. - I just had an arm splint on.

1543
01:02:43,667 --> 01:02:47,836
I was still eager to get jobs in that field.

1544
01:02:47,837 --> 01:02:50,106
- You're a total beast. - Because of that thought,

1545
01:02:50,107 --> 01:02:51,246
- I endured through the pain... - It was a matter of survival.

1546
01:02:51,247 --> 01:02:52,516
- Right. - and kept horseback riding.

1547
01:02:52,517 --> 01:02:53,777
He's a true man.

1548
01:02:54,217 --> 01:02:55,847
He has beastly charms.

1549
01:02:57,087 --> 01:02:59,557
Let's do this. Why did you stop?

1550
01:03:01,657 --> 01:03:02,757
Let's do this.

1551
01:03:02,857 --> 01:03:04,427
(Let's do this.)

1552
01:03:04,727 --> 01:03:05,756
Okay.

1553
01:03:05,757 --> 01:03:08,227
(Terrius sets off once again after making a big resolution.)

1554
01:03:08,557 --> 01:03:09,867
I started getting competitive.

1555
01:03:10,697 --> 01:03:12,596
(We can do this.)

1556
01:03:12,597 --> 01:03:13,667
Out wide.

1557
01:03:15,297 --> 01:03:17,206
There you go. Shoulders back.

1558
01:03:17,207 --> 01:03:18,936
(He moves past the obstacle as if he was one with Cookie.)

1559
01:03:18,937 --> 01:03:20,777
Change direction and go toward the next one.

1560
01:03:21,677 --> 01:03:23,677
- The next one. - This is the tough one.

1561
01:03:25,677 --> 01:03:26,916
This isn't easy to do.

1562
01:03:26,917 --> 01:03:28,017
(He almost fell off at this spot.)

1563
01:03:28,617 --> 01:03:30,516
Change direction and go toward the next one.

1564
01:03:30,517 --> 01:03:31,586
- Slowly. - He did it!

1565
01:03:31,587 --> 01:03:32,657
Slowly.

1566
01:03:33,487 --> 01:03:35,586
One, two, three. There you go.

1567
01:03:35,587 --> 01:03:36,657
(He looks a lot more relaxed now.)

1568
01:03:37,857 --> 01:03:40,757
(Terrius is here on his white horse!)

1569
01:03:41,857 --> 01:03:44,626
Good. Don't speed up.

1570
01:03:44,627 --> 01:03:45,666
(He goes for the next obstacle with a boost of confidence.)

1571
01:03:45,667 --> 01:03:46,796
Two, three.

1572
01:03:46,797 --> 01:03:49,837
Good. Move out wide and aim for the double.

1573
01:03:51,237 --> 01:03:52,776
(He turns naturally.)

1574
01:03:52,777 --> 01:03:54,877
Keep your back straight. Aim for the middle.

1575
01:03:56,277 --> 01:03:57,347
Change.

1576
01:03:58,247 --> 01:03:59,747
Great job.

1577
01:04:00,877 --> 01:04:03,287
(The double jump was done nicely as well.)

1578
01:04:05,717 --> 01:04:06,717
Gosh!

1579
01:04:08,017 --> 01:04:09,056
Look at it.

1580
01:04:09,057 --> 01:04:11,387
"Let's be at the top when it comes to horseback riding."

1581
01:04:11,557 --> 01:04:13,227
I did it with that sort of mindset.

1582
01:04:13,927 --> 01:04:15,096
(To become Korea's number 1)

1583
01:04:15,097 --> 01:04:16,097
There you go.

1584
01:04:16,098 --> 01:04:18,227
Are you planning to be in competitions as well?

1585
01:04:18,367 --> 01:04:19,796
I already competed in one.

1586
01:04:19,797 --> 01:04:20,836
- Really? - What happened?

1587
01:04:20,837 --> 01:04:23,636
- An amateur competition? - I wasn't a pro equestrian...

1588
01:04:23,637 --> 01:04:26,676
and it was for an event match.

1589
01:04:26,677 --> 01:04:28,636
I did compete with others just like in an actual competition.

1590
01:04:28,637 --> 01:04:30,039
- I see. How did you do? - Right.

1591
01:04:30,247 --> 01:04:31,676
Based on my record,

1592
01:04:31,677 --> 01:04:35,017
I think I placed around 3rd to 4th.

1593
01:04:35,177 --> 01:04:36,246
Slowly.

1594
01:04:36,247 --> 01:04:37,346
(He focuses on his training to become number 1.)

1595
01:04:37,347 --> 01:04:39,417
Change. Next one.

1596
01:04:40,057 --> 01:04:42,187
Change. There you go. Move out wide.

1597
01:04:42,557 --> 01:04:43,557
Gosh.

1598
01:04:43,558 --> 01:04:45,427
- That's impressive. - That's really impressive.

1599
01:04:46,397 --> 01:04:48,857
Don't be too fast.

1600
01:04:49,867 --> 01:04:52,427
I rode the horse quite a lot that day.

1601
01:04:52,997 --> 01:04:55,836
Usually, I would be on the horse for a quick session.

1602
01:04:55,837 --> 01:04:57,266
I was on the horse for a quite a while that day.

1603
01:04:57,267 --> 01:04:58,437
(Practicing hard as if it was an actual competition)

1604
01:04:58,837 --> 01:05:01,777
(The effort to become Korea's number 1)

1605
01:05:02,137 --> 01:05:04,707
Go over number 8 and number 1.

1606
01:05:05,247 --> 01:05:06,447
Number two.

1607
01:05:07,147 --> 01:05:08,516
The horse has to be complimented right away.

1608
01:05:08,517 --> 01:05:10,317
- Compliment within three seconds. - Great job.

1609
01:05:10,417 --> 01:05:12,246
Okay. Today's lesson ends here.

1610
01:05:12,247 --> 01:05:14,356
- Great work. - Great work.

1611
01:05:14,357 --> 01:05:15,686
- Gosh, great work, Cookie. - You did well.

1612
01:05:15,687 --> 01:05:17,687
- You did well today. - Gosh, great work.

1613
01:05:19,997 --> 01:05:21,357
(Stopping)

1614
01:05:23,097 --> 01:05:24,091
My legs are shaking.

1615
01:05:26,197 --> 01:05:27,636
(Shaking)

1616
01:05:27,637 --> 01:05:29,367
So your legs shake even after a year of this.

1617
01:05:29,607 --> 01:05:31,167
- Gosh. - Your legs look very nice.

1618
01:05:31,567 --> 01:05:32,577
(Groaning)

1619
01:05:33,477 --> 01:05:34,506
Gosh.

1620
01:05:34,507 --> 01:05:36,677
(The after-effects make him groan automatically.)

1621
01:05:37,347 --> 01:05:38,547
Gosh, look at his legs.

1622
01:05:39,317 --> 01:05:40,647
Are his legs okay?

1623
01:05:42,077 --> 01:05:43,646
- Does it feel like a leg workout? - I guess so.

1624
01:05:43,647 --> 01:05:44,687
Right.

1625
01:05:44,947 --> 01:05:46,856
(Swaying)

1626
01:05:46,857 --> 01:05:48,456
You're like that even after a year of this.

1627
01:05:48,457 --> 01:05:51,857
Goodbye!

1628
01:05:52,697 --> 01:05:55,656
You feel proud after a leg workout.

1629
01:05:55,657 --> 01:05:57,196
- Just like at the gym. - I see.

1630
01:05:57,197 --> 01:05:58,867
Right. That's a great workout.

1631
01:06:02,737 --> 01:06:04,036
("Stigma" by Yim Jae Beom)

1632
01:06:04,037 --> 01:06:05,407
(As if my heart was burnt)

1633
01:06:06,507 --> 01:06:08,876
("For You" by Yim Jae Beom)

1634
01:06:08,877 --> 01:06:11,107
(My wild thoughts and anxious eyes)

1635
01:06:12,377 --> 01:06:15,076
(Woo Il heads back to Seoul while singing Yim Jae Beom's songs.)

1636
01:06:15,077 --> 01:06:17,017
You're back home.

1637
01:06:17,717 --> 01:06:19,317
The navigation will now end.

1638
01:06:20,557 --> 01:06:22,357
(Humming)

1639
01:06:23,587 --> 01:06:24,826
(His hair sways back and forth.)

1640
01:06:24,827 --> 01:06:26,027
He has so much hair.

1641
01:06:28,197 --> 01:06:29,696
(Has he gone to a restaurant?)

1642
01:06:29,697 --> 01:06:30,796
- You went there? - Yes.

1643
01:06:30,797 --> 01:06:31,826
What is this place?

1644
01:06:31,827 --> 01:06:33,467
- This place is... - I should've gone there too.

1645
01:06:33,697 --> 01:06:35,097
really popular.

1646
01:06:35,767 --> 01:06:37,666
(Flustered)

1647
01:06:37,667 --> 01:06:39,107
- It's closed. - I went there too early.

1648
01:06:39,637 --> 01:06:41,907
(Is it not opening time yet?)

1649
01:06:42,337 --> 01:06:43,347
(Surprised)

1650
01:06:43,907 --> 01:06:44,977
What is it?

1651
01:06:46,817 --> 01:06:47,946
It's Yun Hwa.

1652
01:06:47,947 --> 01:06:49,016
(Hong Yun Hwa and Kim Min Gi)

1653
01:06:49,017 --> 01:06:50,747
What was that? Why did you close the door?

1654
01:06:50,947 --> 01:06:52,986
(Min Gi, Yun Hwa)

1655
01:06:52,987 --> 01:06:55,256
(The loveable cutie of the comedy world)

1656
01:06:55,257 --> 01:06:56,287
She's so cute.

1657
01:06:58,327 --> 01:07:01,827
(And a fool for Yun Hwa who only thinks about his wife)

1658
01:07:02,527 --> 01:07:04,296
- They dated for ten years, - That's right.

1659
01:07:04,297 --> 01:07:05,826
and they still love each other so much.

1660
01:07:05,827 --> 01:07:06,896
They're still newlyweds.

1661
01:07:06,897 --> 01:07:08,367
They look at each other with so much love.

1662
01:07:09,407 --> 01:07:10,936
Why did you close the door?

1663
01:07:10,937 --> 01:07:13,007
- Because we're not open yet. - Is that so?

1664
01:07:13,277 --> 01:07:14,377
But it's 12pm.

1665
01:07:15,107 --> 01:07:16,176
We're getting ready.

1666
01:07:16,177 --> 01:07:18,276
- Is that so? - Why are you limping?

1667
01:07:18,277 --> 01:07:20,077
- Did you hurt your legs? - No, I went to ride a horse.

1668
01:07:20,477 --> 01:07:22,147
- What did you do? - Horseback riding.

1669
01:07:22,477 --> 01:07:23,747
- You went horseback riding? - Yes.

1670
01:07:23,887 --> 01:07:25,146
I just got back from it.

1671
01:07:25,147 --> 01:07:27,786
Oh, you get ready to open at this hour.

1672
01:07:27,787 --> 01:07:29,087
We have to get ready to open the bar.

1673
01:07:32,757 --> 01:07:34,197
It's really cute and charming.

1674
01:07:34,457 --> 01:07:38,497
Comedian Kim Min Gi and Hong Yun Hwa...

1675
01:07:39,197 --> 01:07:42,597
are running this bar together.

1676
01:07:43,107 --> 01:07:44,167
Yes.

1677
01:07:44,807 --> 01:07:47,306
Yun Hwa knows I live alone,

1678
01:07:47,307 --> 01:07:48,536
so she always packs side dishes for me.

1679
01:07:48,537 --> 01:07:50,276
She packs me side dishes and soup.

1680
01:07:50,277 --> 01:07:52,207
- Yun Hwa is a good cook. - She packs them for me.

1681
01:07:52,507 --> 01:07:55,577
She always packs the side dishes for me when I go there.

1682
01:07:56,747 --> 01:07:58,386
The bar that Yun Hwa...

1683
01:07:58,387 --> 01:08:00,757
and Min Gi Run is near my place.

1684
01:08:00,857 --> 01:08:03,387
She told me she'd pack me some side dishes,

1685
01:08:03,627 --> 01:08:06,127
so I dropped by on my way home.

1686
01:08:07,097 --> 01:08:08,196
Generally,

1687
01:08:08,197 --> 01:08:11,166
you shouldn't have your hair down at a restaurant.

1688
01:08:11,167 --> 01:08:13,996
When you're at a restaurant, you need to keep your hair neat.

1689
01:08:13,997 --> 01:08:14,997
That's right.

1690
01:08:15,397 --> 01:08:17,836
When the bar opens,

1691
01:08:17,837 --> 01:08:19,606
what does Min Gi do, and what do you do?

1692
01:08:19,607 --> 01:08:20,706
- What are your roles? - I manage the front-of-house.

1693
01:08:20,707 --> 01:08:22,177
- I manage the front-of-house. - I manage the front-of-house.

1694
01:08:22,507 --> 01:08:23,946
- Yun Hwa manages the kitchen. - Right. I manage the kitchen.

1695
01:08:23,947 --> 01:08:25,746
Min Gi manages the outdoor seats and the dining area.

1696
01:08:25,747 --> 01:08:27,516
So your hair can never fall.

1697
01:08:27,517 --> 01:08:28,577
I know.

1698
01:08:29,217 --> 01:08:31,186
- Were you there to help? - That's right.

1699
01:08:31,187 --> 01:08:33,817
I felt bad to get her side dishes for free,

1700
01:08:33,987 --> 01:08:35,756
so I went to help them get ready to open the bar...

1701
01:08:35,757 --> 01:08:38,387
and earn her side dishes.

1702
01:08:38,687 --> 01:08:40,297
I should've worn a hat.

1703
01:08:40,527 --> 01:08:43,367
Even with a hat, people with long hair must tie it tight.

1704
01:08:43,467 --> 01:08:44,897
- I know. - Look at their teamwork.

1705
01:08:45,667 --> 01:08:47,637
- Let me see. How neat. - Is it okay?

1706
01:08:48,297 --> 01:08:49,836
So then my hair won't fall?

1707
01:08:49,837 --> 01:08:51,437
- We're sorry, Jung. - How cute.

1708
01:08:51,837 --> 01:08:52,906
Okay.

1709
01:08:52,907 --> 01:08:54,406
What am I doing today?

1710
01:08:54,407 --> 01:08:56,006
I need to get groceries now.

1711
01:08:56,007 --> 01:08:58,606
- Where do you get your groceries? - Mangwon Market.

1712
01:08:58,607 --> 01:08:59,646
- Oh, Mangwon Market? - It's right there.

1713
01:08:59,647 --> 01:09:00,676
You get your groceries there?

1714
01:09:00,677 --> 01:09:01,817
I see. All right.

1715
01:09:02,177 --> 01:09:03,317
Didn't you bring your jacket?

1716
01:09:03,987 --> 01:09:05,047
It's not cold now.

1717
01:09:05,887 --> 01:09:07,186
We'll have to ride a motorcycle.

1718
01:09:07,187 --> 01:09:08,957
- You'll be cold on it. - Not at all.

1719
01:09:09,187 --> 01:09:10,326
You ride a motorcycle?

1720
01:09:10,327 --> 01:09:11,627
Yes, Yun Hwa rides one.

1721
01:09:12,087 --> 01:09:13,126
How am I supposed to go?

1722
01:09:13,127 --> 01:09:14,197
You can get on the back.

1723
01:09:15,097 --> 01:09:16,367
- At the back of you? - Yes.

1724
01:09:17,767 --> 01:09:18,867
You can get on the back.

1725
01:09:19,467 --> 01:09:21,467
- Wouldn't it be unstable? Really? - Come on, Woo Il.

1726
01:09:21,667 --> 01:09:23,736
- I've ridden it for seven years. - Really?

1727
01:09:23,737 --> 01:09:25,336
- Seven years? Really? - Yes.

1728
01:09:25,337 --> 01:09:26,876
I ride that motorcycle when I go grocery shopping.

1729
01:09:26,877 --> 01:09:28,436
- I feel like she's a good driver. - She is.

1730
01:09:28,437 --> 01:09:30,606
Let's go now. For the opening...

1731
01:09:30,607 --> 01:09:32,277
There are many dishes we need to make in advance.

1732
01:09:33,247 --> 01:09:35,347
- It'll be really cold. - I'll be fine. The wind is...

1733
01:09:36,117 --> 01:09:37,146
It's not cold.

1734
01:09:37,147 --> 01:09:38,347
What? Where is the motorcycle?

1735
01:09:38,517 --> 01:09:39,816
Can both of us ride it?

1736
01:09:39,817 --> 01:09:41,287
(Are you sure the two of us can ride this?)

1737
01:09:42,887 --> 01:09:44,327
- It doesn't... - It doesn't fit?

1738
01:09:44,657 --> 01:09:45,757
All right.

1739
01:09:46,197 --> 01:09:47,357
It's okay. It's right in front.

1740
01:09:48,497 --> 01:09:49,697
Goodness. Wait a minute.

1741
01:09:50,167 --> 01:09:52,367
Min Gi will be unhappy about it.

1742
01:09:53,467 --> 01:09:54,636
- Woo Il! - Woo Il.

1743
01:09:54,637 --> 01:09:55,797
- Grab the back, not Yun Hwa. - I mean...

1744
01:09:56,337 --> 01:09:57,436
- Don't grab her! - He's mad for real.

1745
01:09:57,437 --> 01:09:59,007
- He really is. - He is.

1746
01:09:59,137 --> 01:10:00,777
- I'm a bit anxious. - Come on.

1747
01:10:01,137 --> 01:10:03,677
- I took Gi Ru home on this too. - Really? Okay.

1748
01:10:04,007 --> 01:10:05,107
Drive slowly.

1749
01:10:06,577 --> 01:10:07,816
Check the left side.

1750
01:10:07,817 --> 01:10:09,276
You should check the left side!

1751
01:10:09,277 --> 01:10:11,287
I did!

1752
01:10:11,887 --> 01:10:13,716
- Where are you going? - Look at how he's adoring her.

1753
01:10:13,717 --> 01:10:14,857
That fool for Yun Hwa.

1754
01:10:15,917 --> 01:10:17,657
- See you later. - See you. We'll be right back.

1755
01:10:20,097 --> 01:10:21,997
- I drive a motorcycle really well. - That's good.

1756
01:10:23,067 --> 01:10:24,797
(Exclaiming)

1757
01:10:26,167 --> 01:10:27,337
Go slowly.

1758
01:10:28,037 --> 01:10:29,397
- Come on, Woo Il. - Yes?

1759
01:10:30,007 --> 01:10:31,106
Trust me.

1760
01:10:31,107 --> 01:10:33,807
I've rarely ridden on the back of someone's motorcycle.

1761
01:10:34,037 --> 01:10:35,076
Motorcycle riders don't get on the back, do they?

1762
01:10:35,077 --> 01:10:36,077
No.

1763
01:10:37,447 --> 01:10:39,277
All right. That's great. There you go.

1764
01:10:39,947 --> 01:10:41,077
It's red light.

1765
01:10:41,247 --> 01:10:42,517
Yun Hwa is good.

1766
01:10:43,717 --> 01:10:44,787
That's cute.

1767
01:10:46,187 --> 01:10:48,356
Gosh, don't get too close.

1768
01:10:48,357 --> 01:10:49,527
Gosh, the car is coming.

1769
01:10:49,827 --> 01:10:51,327
- Woo Il, trust me! - Okay.

1770
01:10:52,157 --> 01:10:53,757
You're making me more anxious!

1771
01:10:54,227 --> 01:10:55,556
If you don't drive it, you get nervous.

1772
01:10:55,557 --> 01:10:58,067
If the driver hears that, they become more anxious.

1773
01:10:58,127 --> 01:10:59,297
You have to trust them since you're on it.

1774
01:11:02,297 --> 01:11:04,307
You should check the surroundings for unprotected left turns.

1775
01:11:04,437 --> 01:11:05,736
I did!

1776
01:11:05,737 --> 01:11:08,807
- That means you're not protected. - He sounds just like my mom!

1777
01:11:09,747 --> 01:11:12,046
(A man who knows how to ride a motorcycle)

1778
01:11:12,047 --> 01:11:13,416
- Are you a king of nagging? - You don't know...

1779
01:11:13,417 --> 01:11:14,747
when you might get into an accident.

1780
01:11:14,847 --> 01:11:17,016
You need to make a quick decision.

1781
01:11:17,017 --> 01:11:19,556
- But... - You shouldn't delay at all.

1782
01:11:19,557 --> 01:11:22,617
This is really good. Keeping a distance.

1783
01:11:22,927 --> 01:11:25,957
It's because cars... Yes, you should be careful with these.

1784
01:11:26,057 --> 01:11:28,326
- Be careful. - I'm going at 20km per hour.

1785
01:11:28,327 --> 01:11:29,397
That's it.

1786
01:11:29,767 --> 01:11:31,297
You nag too much.

1787
01:11:31,467 --> 01:11:33,197
I feel like you will make me sick.

1788
01:11:33,537 --> 01:11:34,636
I think I'll get sick.

1789
01:11:34,637 --> 01:11:36,807
Drivers usually don't get carsick.

1790
01:11:37,037 --> 01:11:38,207
- But I feel like I will. - They don't get sick.

1791
01:11:39,237 --> 01:11:41,607
Gosh, look at the fall leaves. My goodness.

1792
01:11:41,707 --> 01:11:42,777
(Blocking his nagging)

1793
01:11:45,107 --> 01:11:48,177
(The leaves turned yellow)

1794
01:11:50,887 --> 01:11:52,116
We're here.

1795
01:11:52,117 --> 01:11:53,286
- It's here. - All right.

1796
01:11:53,287 --> 01:11:55,657
- Mangwon Market. Goodness. - This market is really nice.

1797
01:11:56,017 --> 01:11:57,486
The chili fritter from there is really good.

1798
01:11:57,487 --> 01:11:59,357
Yes, it is. The croquettes are good too.

1799
01:12:00,357 --> 01:12:01,827
What should we buy?

1800
01:12:02,197 --> 01:12:04,497
Onions and fruits.

1801
01:12:05,797 --> 01:12:06,797
(Amazed)

1802
01:12:07,867 --> 01:12:09,397
(Mangwon Market)

1803
01:12:09,937 --> 01:12:11,307
- Gosh. - Gosh.

1804
01:12:11,737 --> 01:12:13,837
- You can't walk past that smell. - I love it.

1805
01:12:14,037 --> 01:12:16,106
(Filled with food that make you salivate)

1806
01:12:16,107 --> 01:12:17,477
Goodness.

1807
01:12:18,177 --> 01:12:20,277
- That's really good. - This is really delicious.

1808
01:12:21,077 --> 01:12:22,177
Goodness.

1809
01:12:22,817 --> 01:12:23,917
- My gosh. - I know.

1810
01:12:24,017 --> 01:12:26,087
(Mangwon Market with 40 years of history has everything.)

1811
01:12:27,487 --> 01:12:28,656
- This is amazing. - Woo Il.

1812
01:12:28,657 --> 01:12:30,027
Seven abalones are ten dollars.

1813
01:12:31,557 --> 01:12:33,896
Our bar used to sell abalones,

1814
01:12:33,897 --> 01:12:35,026
and we got them from here.

1815
