2062
01:21:01,291 --> 01:21:03,190
- Goodness. - Hey.

2063
01:21:03,191 --> 01:21:06,360
We got you something to eat so you could eat right away.

2064
01:21:06,361 --> 01:21:08,731
- Goodness. - We got you something.

2065
01:21:08,861 --> 01:21:10,631
- Do you know how much he spent? - How much?

2066
01:21:11,501 --> 01:21:12,831
He spent more than 50 dollars.

2067
01:21:12,961 --> 01:21:14,201
Goodness.

2068
01:21:14,571 --> 01:21:16,301
- He's become a different man. - He spent more than 50 dollars.

2069
01:21:17,141 --> 01:21:18,270
- He got these? - Yes.

2070
01:21:18,271 --> 01:21:19,400
He spent more than 50 dollars for us.

2071
01:21:19,401 --> 01:21:21,071
No, I didn't pay for everything.

2072
01:21:21,411 --> 01:21:24,310
Hey, I got you this so you could eat it right away.

2073
01:21:24,311 --> 01:21:26,550
This and gimmari. It's really good.

2074
01:21:26,551 --> 01:21:27,580
- Yes. - You like gimmari.

2075
01:21:27,581 --> 01:21:28,611
This gimmari is really good.

2076
01:21:29,081 --> 01:21:31,151
Hey, this sushi. You should have this sushi.

2077
01:21:31,521 --> 01:21:34,751
This couple helped me a lot,

2078
01:21:35,121 --> 01:21:36,621
so I had to pay back.

2079
01:21:36,830 --> 01:21:38,460
- Gosh, it looks good. - Take that out.

2080
01:21:39,121 --> 01:21:41,321
I'll put this in the fridge first.

2081
01:21:42,544 --> 01:21:43,773
It looks good.

2082
01:21:43,861 --> 01:21:46,300
- Gosh, that looks good. - It looks solid.

2083
01:21:46,301 --> 01:21:48,001
(Taking a bite of the sushi Woo Il got for him)

2084
01:21:49,301 --> 01:21:49,903
Woo Il.

2085
01:21:50,801 --> 01:21:52,700
- This... - The radish is delicious.

2086
01:21:52,701 --> 01:21:54,940
Woo Il, did you finish the one I gave you last time?

2087
01:21:54,941 --> 01:21:56,340
- I did. - You did already?

2088
01:21:56,341 --> 01:21:57,541
It's because...

2089
01:21:58,000 --> 01:21:59,830
it's good as a side dish.

2090
01:22:00,081 --> 01:22:01,510
But it goes well with ramyeon too.

2091
01:22:01,511 --> 01:22:02,881
- Right. It's delicious, right? - Yes.

2092
01:22:03,351 --> 01:22:04,623
Then you should take this too.

2093
01:22:04,953 --> 01:22:06,583
What is it? What's that?

2094
01:22:06,721 --> 01:22:07,790
(Bringing a mysterious bag)

2095
01:22:07,791 --> 01:22:09,621
- She's giving so much. - This is...

2096
01:22:09,721 --> 01:22:11,190
- What's this? - Take one each.

2097
01:22:11,191 --> 01:22:12,560
Since you'll be having it by yourself,

2098
01:22:12,561 --> 01:22:14,461
have a fruit each.

2099
01:22:14,761 --> 01:22:15,991
This is fresh kimchi.

2100
01:22:16,131 --> 01:22:17,830
Fresh kimchi? Nice.

2101
01:22:17,831 --> 01:22:19,760
- You must have it today. - Okay.

2102
01:22:19,761 --> 01:22:21,031
This is salted seafood.

2103
01:22:21,701 --> 01:22:23,600
- Salted seafood? What kind? - I packed a bit of everything.

2104
01:22:23,601 --> 01:22:25,300
- This is salted octopus. - Oh, there are different kinds.

2105
01:22:25,301 --> 01:22:27,210
This is salted pollack roe, and this is salted pollack intestine.

2106
01:22:27,211 --> 01:22:28,610
This is seasoned raw pollack.

2107
01:22:28,611 --> 01:22:29,670
How generous of her.

2108
01:22:29,671 --> 01:22:32,511
She packed it appropriately for people who live alone.

2109
01:22:32,881 --> 01:22:34,411
This is from Jeju.

2110
01:22:34,651 --> 01:22:37,480
You know the thing that was modified with hwanggeumhyang.

2111
01:22:37,481 --> 01:22:38,820
Goodness, that's precious.

2112
01:22:38,821 --> 01:22:40,290
You should have one per day only.

2113
01:22:40,291 --> 01:22:41,590
You have high blood sugar.

2114
01:22:41,591 --> 01:22:42,790
She's worried about his high blood sugar too.

2115
01:22:42,791 --> 01:22:44,321
All right, thank you.

2116
01:22:45,391 --> 01:22:46,490
Take this too.

2117
01:22:46,491 --> 01:22:48,231
- A foam roller? - Yes, that.

2118
01:22:48,491 --> 01:22:50,600
- Take this too. - She's giving everything.

2119
01:22:50,601 --> 01:22:52,130
That must cost more than 50 dollars.

2120
01:22:52,131 --> 01:22:53,930
Yun Hwa is really generous.

2121
01:22:53,931 --> 01:22:55,071
He's taking twice as much.

2122
01:22:55,671 --> 01:22:57,840
Hey, this is too much. It's really fine.

2123
01:22:57,841 --> 01:22:59,441
Gosh, lucky I got paper towels.

2124
01:22:59,501 --> 01:23:00,540
(The bag is already full.)

2125
01:23:00,541 --> 01:23:02,970
We should hold a flea market someday.

2126
01:23:02,971 --> 01:23:04,610
For real. Don't just talk.

2127
01:23:04,611 --> 01:23:05,680
I'm serious.

2128
01:23:05,681 --> 01:23:07,150
Really? Then are you willing to take some?

2129
01:23:07,151 --> 01:23:08,980
Of course. For sure.

2130
01:23:08,981 --> 01:23:11,420
Don't we have a lot of stuff that he must want?

2131
01:23:11,421 --> 01:23:13,120
- All of us have a lot. - We...

2132
01:23:13,121 --> 01:23:14,791
have so much stuff.

2133
01:23:15,251 --> 01:23:17,521
- We must share them. - We really should.

2134
01:23:17,591 --> 01:23:20,261
- Take this bag like this, okay? - Okay.

2135
01:23:21,231 --> 01:23:22,460
I'll get going.

2136
01:23:22,461 --> 01:23:24,700
Woo Il, please help him clean.

2137
01:23:24,701 --> 01:23:25,731
- Me? - Okay.

2138
01:23:25,901 --> 01:23:27,400
- I'll get going. - Where is she going?

2139
01:23:27,401 --> 01:23:30,071
Yun Hwa had some work.

2140
01:23:31,341 --> 01:23:33,441
There are spiderwebs between the gaps.

2141
01:23:34,011 --> 01:23:36,611
Oh, here? Like this?

2142
01:23:36,811 --> 01:23:39,641
Roll the spiderwebs with this to remove them.

2143
01:23:40,411 --> 01:23:41,950
I was trying to help.

2144
01:23:41,951 --> 01:23:43,320
- You should earn your keep. - Oh, like these?

2145
01:23:43,321 --> 01:23:46,621
You need a health certificate to work at a restaurant.

2146
01:23:46,721 --> 01:23:49,021
I got one, actually.

2147
01:23:49,251 --> 01:23:50,721
I have to insert a cotton swab...

2148
01:23:51,191 --> 01:23:53,830
into your anus 3cm deep and remove it.

2149
01:23:53,831 --> 01:23:55,460
That must hurt a lot.

2150
01:23:55,461 --> 01:23:56,630
It's also my wonder...

2151
01:23:56,631 --> 01:24:00,201
why that is the only way to check for typhoid.

2152
01:24:00,301 --> 01:24:01,800
Thanks to them, you checked to see if you had typhoid.

2153
01:24:01,801 --> 01:24:02,930
You passed.

2154
01:24:02,931 --> 01:24:04,001
(Thanks to them, he got to check that he's healthy.)

2155
01:24:04,901 --> 01:24:06,370
It's nice that you're helping.

2156
01:24:06,371 --> 01:24:08,041
- Right. - We get to prepare for winter.

2157
01:24:08,811 --> 01:24:10,310
This is quite pleasing.

2158
01:24:10,311 --> 01:24:11,341
That's right.

2159
01:24:12,211 --> 01:24:15,450
He said they got spiderwebs quicker than they thought.

2160
01:24:15,451 --> 01:24:17,120
- I can see. - They get it in a day?

2161
01:24:17,121 --> 01:24:20,621
They keep getting them after a day.

2162
01:24:21,291 --> 01:24:23,190
- Gosh. For real. - It's all good.

2163
01:24:23,191 --> 01:24:25,420
(Thanks to Woo Il, it's become clean.)

2164
01:24:25,421 --> 01:24:27,761
- It's clean. Oh, my. - There are many gaps.

2165
01:24:28,931 --> 01:24:30,631
(Brushing)

2166
01:24:31,201 --> 01:24:33,771
(He cleans the street in front of the bar as well.)

2167
01:24:35,831 --> 01:24:37,170
(Thanks to him, it becomes clean.)

2168
01:24:37,171 --> 01:24:38,901
He's diligent and good.

2169
01:24:39,841 --> 01:24:41,011
There you go.

2170
01:24:41,971 --> 01:24:44,411
(Brushing the sidewalk blocks with a brush as well)

2171
01:24:45,441 --> 01:24:48,311
There were a lot of bird droppings as there was a tree.

2172
01:24:50,081 --> 01:24:53,151
It's a sidewalk in front of the bar,

2173
01:24:53,251 --> 01:24:55,390
so some people wait in line on that sidewalk.

2174
01:24:55,391 --> 01:24:57,260
- If they see bird droppings, - Right.

2175
01:24:57,261 --> 01:24:59,421
- it might not look hygienic. - Right.

2176
01:25:01,531 --> 01:25:03,430
Woo Il is good.

2177
01:25:03,431 --> 01:25:04,431
(Brushing harder than anyone)

2178
01:25:05,201 --> 01:25:07,630
Shouldn't I be rewarded by the district office at this rate?

2179
01:25:07,631 --> 01:25:09,770
I got more eager to clean as it got cleaner.

2180
01:25:09,771 --> 01:25:11,840
Woo Il did most of the work on the field day too.

2181
01:25:11,841 --> 01:25:13,240
There are so many bird droppings.

2182
01:25:13,241 --> 01:25:14,911
(Working hard)

2183
01:25:15,211 --> 01:25:16,640
(Surprised)

2184
01:25:16,641 --> 01:25:18,141
- It's good, right? Okay. - Yes.

2185
01:25:18,341 --> 01:25:19,680
- It's clean. - It's neat.

2186
01:25:19,681 --> 01:25:21,210
- Yes. - For real.

2187
01:25:21,211 --> 01:25:22,311
It's clean.

2188
01:25:22,581 --> 01:25:25,321
(He continues to clean the inside as well.)

2189
01:25:25,981 --> 01:25:27,590
He helped a lot.

2190
01:25:27,591 --> 01:25:28,821
(Cleaning every table without missing one)

2191
01:25:29,491 --> 01:25:31,461
(Cleaning the sides thoroughly as well)

2192
01:25:32,261 --> 01:25:33,660
(A part-timer who takes care of things on his own)

2193
01:25:33,661 --> 01:25:35,661
Normally, people sit on the inside first.

2194
01:25:36,461 --> 01:25:38,231
I'm really happy these days.

2195
01:25:38,561 --> 01:25:40,370
It was tiring to go horseback riding...

2196
01:25:40,371 --> 01:25:42,871
and help Yun Hwa and Min Gi,

2197
01:25:43,171 --> 01:25:47,241
But this is also proof that I've changed.

2198
01:25:47,971 --> 01:25:51,111
I can be that generous, at least.

2199
01:25:52,211 --> 01:25:55,811
Today was tiring, but it was filling.

2200
01:25:56,511 --> 01:25:57,921
That's what I thought.

2201
01:25:58,781 --> 01:26:00,490
I'll get going. Thanks for this!

2202
01:26:00,491 --> 01:26:01,590
- Bye, Woo Il. - Bye. Thank you.

2203
01:26:01,591 --> 01:26:02,790
Thank you so much.

2204
01:26:02,791 --> 01:26:05,021
- I'll text Yun Hwa. Thank you. - Okay.

2205
01:26:05,861 --> 01:26:06,891
Bye.

2206
01:26:08,291 --> 01:26:09,590
You're taking so much stuff.

2207
01:26:09,591 --> 01:26:11,560
- He helped a lot, though. - Bye!

2208
01:26:11,561 --> 01:26:13,261
He cleaned outside and inside as well.

2209
01:26:15,031 --> 01:26:17,941
(This is the Class of Terrius)

2210
01:26:18,841 --> 01:26:20,371
(Next story)

2211
01:26:20,971 --> 01:26:22,211
(The day she went to clean her grandparents' place)

2212
01:26:23,111 --> 01:26:25,381
(She shared her worry with Hyun Moo and Kian84.)

2213
01:26:26,541 --> 01:26:27,780
(You should keep him.)

2214
01:26:27,781 --> 01:26:28,781
(I'll help you.)

2215
01:26:30,281 --> 01:26:31,820
(With their sincere support,)

2216
01:26:31,821 --> 01:26:33,921
(Na Rae plucked up her courage.)

2217
01:26:34,891 --> 01:26:36,521
(Introducing Na Rae's new family)

2218
01:26:37,521 --> 01:26:39,591
(It's been two months and a half since they started living together.)

2219
01:26:41,731 --> 01:26:43,261
(The house is already filled with Bok Dol's stuff.)

2220
01:26:43,861 --> 01:26:45,300
(I think my dog...)

2221
01:26:45,301 --> 01:26:46,661
(is a genius.)

2222
01:26:47,131 --> 01:26:48,301
(He's really smart.)

2223
01:26:48,501 --> 01:26:49,571
Wait.

2224
01:26:49,631 --> 01:26:50,641
(Focused)

2225
01:26:51,001 --> 01:26:52,170
(Good job!)

2226
01:26:52,171 --> 01:26:53,171
(You smart dog!)

2227
01:26:53,771 --> 01:26:55,111
(Let's get you dressed, my genius dog.)

2228
01:26:55,841 --> 01:26:57,741
(I can't miss out on styling my dog.)

2229
01:26:58,311 --> 01:26:59,410
(It's really cute.)

2230
01:26:59,411 --> 01:27:00,481
(Shall we try it on?)

2231
01:27:00,911 --> 01:27:03,051
(You'll become the best dog.)

2232
01:27:04,151 --> 01:27:05,521
(Your food will have to be special too.)

2233
01:27:06,251 --> 01:27:07,921
(I'll give you the best of the best things.)

2234
01:27:09,151 --> 01:27:10,891
(It's time for tutoring.)

2235
01:27:11,621 --> 01:27:12,891
(Just fully trust me.)

2236
01:27:13,591 --> 01:27:15,790
(For my dog,)

2237
01:27:15,791 --> 01:27:17,801
(I can do this much.)

2238
01:27:21,301 --> 01:27:22,771
(I'm dog tired.)

2239
01:27:23,431 --> 01:27:24,641
It's a mess.

2240
01:27:24,871 --> 01:27:27,671
(Sky Castle for Dogs)

2241
01:27:28,811 --> 01:27:30,341
(Ji Hyeon is opening a box?)

2242
01:27:31,141 --> 01:27:32,649
(He took out a skate from it?)

2243
01:27:33,848 --> 01:27:36,188
(Today, he's hosting an important guest.)

2244
01:27:36,548 --> 01:27:37,558
(Hitting)

2245
01:27:38,458 --> 01:27:39,458
(Skillful)

2246
01:27:40,288 --> 01:27:42,028
(Skillfully showing off how to prepare a skate)

2247
01:27:42,528 --> 01:27:44,228
(Here comes Park Skate.)

2248
01:27:45,628 --> 01:27:46,658
(Gosh, it's so nice.)

2249
01:27:48,198 --> 01:27:49,628
(All kinds of delicacies from Mokpo are here.)

2250
01:27:50,568 --> 01:27:52,698
(Filling the container with love for the important guest)

2251
01:27:53,768 --> 01:27:55,267
(Packing a bundle is no problem.)

2252
01:27:55,268 --> 01:27:57,108
(Taking care of his looks is also no problem.)

2253
01:27:57,738 --> 01:28:00,248
(The place he reached after packing so much stuff)

2254
01:28:01,348 --> 01:28:02,608
(The important guest can be seen from afar.)

2255
01:28:03,448 --> 01:28:04,578
(Bowing)

2256
01:28:05,178 --> 01:28:06,348
How have you been?

2257
01:28:06,578 --> 01:28:07,818
(It's Ji Hyun's idol, Singer Nam Jin.)

2258
01:28:08,588 --> 01:28:10,048
(It's the 60th year since his debut.)

2259
01:28:10,158 --> 01:28:11,558
The living legend.

2260
01:28:12,218 --> 01:28:14,428
(The first dance singer of Korea)

2261
01:28:14,858 --> 01:28:16,128
(You'd be a spy if you don't know him.)

2262
01:28:16,958 --> 01:28:18,457
(The representative singer from Mokpo, Ji Hyeon's hometown,)

2263
01:28:18,458 --> 01:28:19,698
(Nam Jin)

2264
01:28:20,268 --> 01:28:21,328
(You're quite tall.)

2265
01:28:21,928 --> 01:28:23,068
(Awkward)

2266
01:28:23,368 --> 01:28:24,768
(You have the right attitude.)

2267
01:28:25,338 --> 01:28:27,138
(Becoming naturally polite at the godfather's charisma)

2268
01:28:27,508 --> 01:28:28,538
(You haven't eaten yet?)

2269
01:28:28,908 --> 01:28:30,338
(I didn't, so I can eat this a lot.)

2270
01:28:31,878 --> 01:28:33,707
(It's long-arm octopus.)

2271
01:28:33,708 --> 01:28:34,708
(Or three-legged octopus.)

2272
01:28:34,848 --> 01:28:35,848
(Pardon?)

2273
01:28:36,278 --> 01:28:37,917
(The senior's dazzling wit...)

2274
01:28:37,918 --> 01:28:39,748
(keeps coming without pause.)

2275
01:28:40,518 --> 01:28:41,518
(Polite)

2276
01:28:42,518 --> 01:28:43,858
(And...)

2277
01:28:44,258 --> 01:28:45,458
(Glaring)

2278
01:28:46,158 --> 01:28:47,458
(He ended up making a mistake?)

2279
01:28:48,188 --> 01:28:49,387
(With My Dear)

2280
01:28:49,388 --> 01:28:51,698
(With My Charismatic Senior)
